# Agent Workflow Protocol (MANDATORY)

## Purpose
This document defines the REQUIRED workflow for AI agents working with the Nucleus Brain. It prevents the failure pattern of "ad-hoc work → claim victory → find more tasks when pushed".

## The Core Rule
**The Brain drives work. Work does not Update the brain retroactively.**

---

## Session Start Protocol (REQUIRED)

Every work session MUST begin with these steps:

### 1. Call [brain_session_start()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3976-4110)
This tool returns:
- Current satellite view
- Top 5 pending tasks by priority
- Active sprint (if any)
- Session recommendations

**If this tool shows Priority 1-2 tasks, you MUST work on those first** unless user explicitly overrides.

### 2. Confirm Sprint
- If there's an active sprint, stay focused on it
- If no sprint and starting significant work, call [brain_save_session()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2341-2362) to create one
- If user request conflicts with sprint, SHOW THEM THE CONFLICT and let them decide

### 3. Claim Task (for multi-agent systems)
- If working in parallel with other agents, call [brain_claim_task()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2525-2537)
- This prevents race conditions

---

## During Work Protocol

### Check Before Claiming "Done"
Before saying "this is complete" or "ready for next task":

1. Call [brain_list_tasks(status="PENDING")](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2493-2512)
2. Verify your work actually completed a task
3. Update that task: [brain_update_task(task_id, {"status": "DONE"})](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2500-2512)

### Never Claim Victory Without Brain Confirmation
❌ WRONG: "GenAI migration complete!"
✅ RIGHT: Query Brain tasks, see 9 pending, report honestly

---

## Session End Protocol

### When User Says "What's Left?"
1. Call [brain_list_tasks(status="PENDING")](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2493-2512)
2. Call [brain_satellite_view()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3310-3325)
3. Report EXACTLY what the Brain says, not what you remember working on

### When Finishing Work
1. Update task status in Brain
2. Call [brain_save_session()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2341-2362) if significant work was done
3. Return current status from Brain, not your opinion

---

## Context Hygiene (Anti-Hallucination)

- Do NOT infer active tasks from open browser tabs. Treat tabs as passive context only. Ask before creating tasks.

## Tool-First Execution (No Suggestion Mode)

**RULE:** When work needs to be done, **USE THE TOOL**. Do not describe what *could* be done.

| Scenario | ❌ Wrong (Suggestion) | ✅ Right (Execution) |
|:---------|:---------------------|:--------------------|
| New task identified | "You could add a task..." | [brain_add_task()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2551-2572) |
| Task completed | "This task is done..." | [brain_update_task(status=DONE)](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2500-2512) |
| Important event | "This should be logged..." | [brain_emit_event()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2439-2443) |
| Session ending | "You might want to save..." | [brain_save_session()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2341-2362) |
| Commitment found | "There's a TODO here..." | [brain_scan_commitments()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3330-3346) |

**Rationale:** The Brain is only useful if it reflects reality. Suggestions create drift. Execution creates truth.

